DocFlow API - Reliability Implementation Changes
Date: 2026-03-03

============================================================
1) SUMMARY OF WHAT WAS IMPLEMENTED
============================================================
This update implemented four reliability pillars across the API + Celery workflow:

1. Dual-Write Recovery (Outbox/Sweeper pattern)
2. Idempotent Worker Processing
3. AI Circuit Breaker for graceful degradation
4. Distributed Tracing via Correlation IDs

It also added targeted reliability tests and database migration support.


============================================================
2) DETAILED CHANGES BY REQUIREMENT
============================================================

A) Dual-Write Problem (Partial Failures)
----------------------------------------
Problem addressed:
- API submits a job and writes to multiple systems (S3/MinIO, PostgreSQL, Redis/Celery).
- If DB write succeeds but Celery dispatch fails, jobs can remain stuck forever.

What was implemented:
1. Added periodic sweeper task:
   - File: api/src/tasks/sweep_pending_jobs.py
   - Task: sweep_stuck_jobs_task
   - Behavior:
     - Runs every 5 minutes.
     - Queries jobs stuck in PENDING or QUEUED_AI_OUTAGE for >10 minutes.
     - Re-dispatches jobs safely to Celery when circuit is closed.
     - Increments enqueue_attempts and updates last_enqueued_at.

2. Registered sweeper in Celery beat schedule:
   - File: api/src/tasks/celery_app.py
   - Added beat_schedule entry:
     - sweep-stuck-pending-jobs
     - cron: every 5 minutes

3. Added tracking fields for observability:
   - File: api/src/jobs/models.py
   - New columns:
     - enqueue_attempts (int)
     - last_enqueued_at (datetime, nullable)


B) Idempotency (Safe Retries)
-----------------------------
Problem addressed:
- Celery retries can re-run the same job and waste cost or overwrite final state.

What was implemented:
1. Idempotency guard in worker:
   - File: api/src/tasks/process_job.py
   - Before expensive processing, worker checks:
     - if job.status is COMPLETE/COMPLETED -> return immediately.

2. Retry behavior keeps terminal consistency:
   - FAILED during retries
   - DEAD after max retries
   - completed_at set for terminal dead path


C) Circuit Breaker (Graceful Degradation)
-----------------------------------------
Problem addressed:
- AI provider outage causes retry storms and infrastructure thrashing.

What was implemented:
1. Circuit breaker constants/helpers:
   - File: api/src/jobs/reliability.py
   - Keys/constants:
     - AI_BREAKER_FAILURE_KEY
     - AI_BREAKER_OPEN_UNTIL_KEY
     - AI_BREAKER_FAILURE_THRESHOLD = 5
     - AI_BREAKER_OPEN_SECONDS = 600
   - Also includes sweep timing constants and UTC helper.

2. Worker-side breaker logic:
   - File: api/src/tasks/process_job.py
   - Behavior:
     - Detect AI/upstream failures.
     - Count consecutive failures in Redis.
     - Trip circuit after threshold and open for 10 minutes.
     - Mark affected jobuccesss as QUEUED_AI_OUTAGE instead of retry storming.
     - Reset failure counter after sful AI call.

3. Submit-time breaker awareness:
   - File: api/src/routers/jobs.py
   - On incoming job:
     - If circuit is open, save as QUEUED_AI_OUTAGE and do not dispatch task.
     - If closed, normal PENDING + immediate dispatch.

4. Added new status value:
   - File: api/src/jobs/enums.py
   - Added: QUEUED_AI_OUTAGE


D) Distributed Tracing (Correlation IDs)
----------------------------------------
Problem addressed:
- Hard to follow one request across API, storage, DB, and worker logs.

What was implemented:
1. Correlation ID generation at request entry:
   - File: api/src/routers/jobs.py
   - UUID created at start of submit_job.

2. Correlation ID persisted in DB:
   - File: api/src/jobs/models.py
   - New column: correlation_id (indexed, non-null)

3. Correlation ID propagated into storage:
   - File: api/src/services/storage.py
   - upload_to_s3 now accepts correlation_id
   - S3 object key includes correlation segment
   - Object metadata includes correlation_id

4. Correlation ID propagated into task dispatch:
   - File: api/src/routers/jobs.py
   - Celery task called with args [job_id, correlation_id]

5. Correlation ID exposed to clients:
   - File: api/src/jobs/schemas.py
   - Added correlation_id in JobResponse and JobStatusResponse


