============================================================
4) DATABASE / MIGRATION DETAILS
============================================================
Migration file:
- alembic/versions/9b2f5d5d7a11_add_reliability_fields_and_queue_status.py

Upgrade actions:
- Add enum value: QUEUED_AI_OUTAGE
- Add columns to jobs:
  - enqueue_attempts (default 0)
  - correlation_id (nullable then backfilled from id::text, then set NOT NULL)
  - last_enqueued_at (nullable)
- Create index ix_jobs_correlation_id

Downgrade actions:
- Drop index and newly added columns
(Note: enum value removal is intentionally not attempted in downgrade.)


============================================================
5) TESTING ADDED
============================================================
Added tests in:
- tests/test_reliability.py

Scenarios covered:
1. process_job_task idempotent skip if already complete
2. process_job_task marks queued during open circuit
3. sweep_stuck_jobs_task requeues stale jobs and increments enqueue_attempts
4. submit_job propagates correlation ID to storage + DB + Celery dispatch
5. submit_job queues without dispatch when breaker is open


============================================================
6) OPERATIONAL DOs (IMPORTANT)
============================================================
1. Run migration before deploy:
   alembic upgrade head

2. Run both worker and beat:
   - Celery worker handles processing
   - Celery beat runs sweeper every 5 minutes

3. Monitor these Redis keys:
   - docflow:ai:breaker:consecutive_failures
   - docflow:ai:breaker:open_until

4. Track job statuses and alert if too many stale queued jobs:
   - PENDING
   - QUEUED_AI_OUTAGE

5. Use correlation_id when searching logs and debugging incidents.


